{
  "_comment": [
    "The external kits this instance composes, one entry per remote source.",
    "This is the single list both sides read: `just services-pin <kit> <digest>` takes the image and public key from here to write the profile's services.sources[] entry, and the e2e seed derives its bundled expectations from the marketplaces listed here (playwright/tests/support/services-yaml.ts). Nothing is hand-typed twice.",
    "A kit's marketplace, plugins and skills live in the kit's repository; who reaches them is declared in services/access-control/rules.yaml with `owner: bundle:<name>`.",
    "status: pinned \u2014 the profile pins this kit (or is expected to); the seed asserts its marketplaces are served. planned \u2014 the kit repository is being seeded (`just kit-export`); its ids still live in services/ until it is pinned, so the seed ignores it.",
    "pull: public \u2014 the GHCR package is public, so the profile entry carries no auth_secret. channel \u2014 the tag the kit's CI moves on every release; `just services-pin <kit> <channel>` follows it, `just services-pin <kit> sha256:<digest>` pins one upload."
  ],
